Subject: [PATCH] docs: CHANGELOG and FINDINGS - the public trail a stranger
 can actually read

Upstream keeps no changelog; it versions by build-number tag and carries the narrative in
pull requests and issues on GitHub. A fork cannot rely on that: the reader's first question
is what changed and on what base, and a rebase can change behaviour with no code change of
ours. CHANGELOG.md is grouped by upstream base for exactly that reason.

FINDINGS.md is the research log - defects, format findings, measured losses and open
questions, each with its reproduction. It publishes the negatives on purpose: on a fork
whose pitch is that everything is measured, a missing negative is a missing result.

Both files name the hardware on every number and keep losses in the table beside the wins.

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-110D, public-release bar
Measured-effect: documentation only; no engine behaviour changed.
